<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Weekly crawl, run unattended.

  STILL NOT INSTALLED, deliberately - see "Why it stays uninstalled" below.
  Nothing is scheduled until someone runs the launchctl load command.

  FIXED 18 September 2026. As written it could not have worked, in three
  separate ways, and because it was never loaded none of them ever surfaced:

    1. It ran `npm run crawl:refresh`. There is no such script - and never
       was. The crawl is `monitor:run`.
    2. It cd'd to "$HOME/offerly-site", which is not where this repository
       lives.
    3. It called npm at "$HOME/.local/node-v24.19.0-darwin-arm64/bin/npm",
       which does not exist on this machine. Node is installed via nvm.

  So there has never been a scheduled crawl. Every crawl to date has been run
  by hand, and the old comment below about the schedule "burning API budget"
  was wrong on top of that: a crawl makes no API-keyed calls at all. It hits
  free, unauthenticated ATS and careers endpoints plus headless Chromium, and
  spends zero Anthropic tokens. Measured by tracing monitor-run.ts's imports -
  the only LLM path in the monitoring code, llm-extract.ts, is reachable just
  from the manual backfill-eligibility.ts.

  Install:
    cp scripts/com.offerly.crawl-refresh.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.offerly.crawl-refresh.plist

  Uninstall:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.offerly.crawl-refresh.plist

  Runs Sundays at 04:15: crawls every due source, publishes whatever the
  classifier auto-approved (which now also alerts the students watching that
  firm), then spends a capped 25 model calls filling in eligibility the
  deterministic parser could not read.

  That last step is the ONLY thing here that costs money, and it is
  deliberately a separate step rather than part of the crawl. The crawl itself
  stays free and deterministic, third-party posting text reaches a model only
  in this bounded pass, and a prompt change can be re-run over the same stored
  rows without re-fetching a single careers page - all three of which are
  properties backfill-eligibility.ts's own header asks for. --limit 25 keeps
  a week's spend to 25 Haiku calls whatever the crawl turned up.

  Weekly rather than daily is the right cadence:
  firms publish a deadline once, months ahead, so a daily sweep spends ~7x the
  requests to learn the same thing. The per-source tiers inside monitor-run
  already check the urgent boards far more often than this when run by hand.

  WHY IT STAYS UNINSTALLED
  ------------------------
  PGlite is single-writer. If this fires while the dev server is up, the two
  processes contend for one data directory, which is how this repository lost
  a database on 18 September 2026.

  That is now caught rather than hoped about: the guard in
  src/lib/monitoring/exclusive-db.ts connects to the dev port and the crawl
  refuses to start. So the failure mode is no longer corruption - it is a
  silently SKIPPED weekly run every week you happen to leave the server
  running, with the reason only in the log below.

  Install it once the app is on real Postgres (next step #7), which removes the
  constraint entirely. Until then, running it by hand is the honest option.

  NOTE: the npm path below is nvm's current version. If Node is upgraded, this
  breaks silently - launchd will log "no such file or directory" to the error
  log and nothing else will tell you.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.offerly.crawl-refresh</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd "/Users/kaiclauson/Developer/Offerly Bing Bong" &amp;&amp; export PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.19.0/bin:$PATH" &amp;&amp; npm run monitor:run -- --limit 110 &amp;&amp; npx tsx --env-file=.env.local --conditions=react-server scripts/promote-approved-listings.ts &amp;&amp; npx tsx --env-file=.env.local --conditions=react-server scripts/backfill-eligibility.ts --limit 25 --apply</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Weekday</key><integer>0</integer>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>15</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/offerly-crawl-refresh.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/offerly-crawl-refresh.err.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
